{
  "summary": "This commit removes the 'type' column from tasks table INSERTs across multiple services and makes a critical bug change to AgentSessionService (radix 10 → 3 in parseInt). The schema change appears intentional but lacks a migration.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "NEVER change the radix parameter in parseInt. The second argument is the number base (10 for decimal). Changing from 10 to 3 will cause parseInt('3', 3) to return NaN and parseInt('10', 3) to return 3. Always use radix 10 for decimal numbers."
    },
    {
      "topic": "SQL migrations",
      "reminder": "When removing a column from application code, always create a corresponding migration to drop the column from the database. Schema changes without migrations will cause runtime errors."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Arrow function style",
      "reminder": "The change from `(item) => ({...})` to `item => ({...})` is purely stylistic. Both work identically. Don't make style-only changes in bug-fix commits."
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "critical",
      "file": "src/services/AgentSessionService.ts:24",
      "issue": "parseInt radix changed from 10 to 3",
      "detail": "This is a functional bug. `parseInt('3', 3)` returns NaN, `parseInt('10', 3)` returns 3. Should always use radix 10 for decimal parsing."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/cli/index.ts, MeetingHandler.ts, ReviewService.ts",
      "issue": "Removed 'type' column from tasks table without migration",
      "detail": "The 'type' column was removed from INSERT statements but the database schema still expects it. This will cause SQL errors at runtime unless a migration was run separately."
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "file": "src/services/AgentSessionService.ts:24",
      "suggestion": "Revert radix to 10: `parseInt(process.env.NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS ?? '3', 10)`"
    },
    {
      "file": "Database",
      "suggestion": "Create migration to drop 'type' column from tasks table: `ALTER TABLE tasks DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS type;`"
    },
    {
      "file": "All files",
      "suggestion": "Separate schema changes into their own commits with migrations"
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Consistent removal of deprecated 'type' column across all INSERT locations",
    "Minor arrow function cleanup shows attention to code style"
  ],
  "overallScore": 40,
  "codeQualityScore": 50,
  "testCoverageScore": 0,
  "documentationScore": 0
}

